{"ratings":[{"id":"C1","consequence":"boundary","trigger":"plausible","reason":"An unrelated orphan started in the same worktree can be mistaken for an invocation descendant and killed."},{"id":"C2","consequence":"boundary","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A detached descendant with a replaced environment and an outside working directory can survive confirmed shutdown and keep writing to the checkout."},{"id":"C3","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A transient cleanup failure during a gate-timeout rerun terminates the run instead of recovering."},{"id":"C2b","consequence":"boundary","trigger":"plausible","reason":"On Linux, a same-group helper with a replaced environment can escape shutdown and continue writing during later work."}]}